> Wouldn't "zukte ro lo se kakne be se va'u do" work?

Yes, it would.

The difference is just between doing and bringing about. The one I went 
with ({gasnu ro lo jai se kakne}, which means {gasnu ro lo jai se kakne 
be se va'u do bei fai lo ka gasnu}), says that he'll bring about all the 
things he can bring about, possibly including things he can't do 
himself, so I think I prefer gasnu in this case. That is not to say that 
{zukte} wouldn't work, of course.

